<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">encumbrance</ansi>

When you personally carry more objects than your strength permits, you
become encumbered.

Check your inventory to see how many objects you can carry.

This is separate from your company's shared cargo load, which is
weighed in grams rather than counted in objects, and covers your
companions' gear and cargo too, not just your own pack (<ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>).
Being encumbered yourself and your company being overloaded can happen
independently of each other.

When encumbered, each step costs you far more effort (five times as much), so you tire quickly on the move.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help cargo</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help strain</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help inventory</ansi>.
